## 1. Objective restatement and acceptance surface (traceability)

Produce, at IMPLEMENT, one report — `reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md` — containing a
hand-extraction attempt against **3 real sealed goals** drawn from `ledger/` and `reviews/tasks/`,
targeting the SAEOS-1 §4.3 node types, grading every field `extractable` / `partial` / `absent`,
closing with an explicit **GO** or **NO-GO** and a loss ratio.

The probe falsifies (or fails to falsify) **SAEOS-1 §9/A8**: *does PAEOS emit clean structured
decisions?* Per **§10/D7**, S1 is *"explicitly a falsification test, not a build"*.

The four acceptance checks bind the report's **byte-level shape** and are therefore treated as
interface requirements, frozen in §3.5:

| # | Check (verbatim) | Binding |
|---|---|---|
| AC-1 | `test -f reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md` | Exact path; `reviews/spikes/` must exist at emit time. |
| AC-2 | `rg -q '^verdict: (GO\|NO-GO)$' …` | One column-0 `verdict:` line, one of two tokens, no trailing whitespace. |
| AC-3 | `test $(rg -c '^## goal: ' …) -ge 3` | ≥3 column-0 `## goal: ` lines. A zero-match `rg -c` exits 1 and prints nothing, making `test` receive an empty operand and error — the emitter must guarantee ≥3. |
| AC-4 | `rg -q '^loss_ratio: 0\.[0-9]+$' …` | One column-0 `loss_ratio:` line whose value **must begin `0.`**. See §6.1 — this regex cannot express `1.0`. |

This restates DESIGN §1 without adding, relaxing, or reinterpreting any requirement.

